  "result": "I fixed `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. `click.IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True).convert('0', None, None)` now returns 1 instead of -1.\n\n`_clamp` was returning `bound - dir`. The caller passes `dir=1` for the minimum and `dir=-1` for the maximum, so for open bounds it moved away from the valid range. It now returns `bound + dir`.\n\nI added four regression cases to the clamp parametrize list at the top of `tests/test_types.py`:\n- **Open minimum:** `\"0\"` and `\"-5\"` both clamp to 1.\n- **Open maximum:** `\"5\"` and `\"9\"` both clamp to 4.\n\n`python -m pytest tests/test_types.py -q` gives 45 passed, 2 skipped. I didn't run the full suite or check why the two tests are skipped.",
